## Develop
{% if language == 'python' %}
```sh
uv sync                     # install (creates .venv and uv.lock; commit uv.lock)
uv run pytest               # tests
uv run pre-commit install   # checks on every commit
```
{% else %}
```sh
brew install xcodegen swiftformat swiftlint pre-commit
xcodegen generate                # makes {{ app_name }}.xcodeproj from project.yml
open {{ app_name }}.xcodeproj
pre-commit install               # checks on every commit
```

CI pins swiftformat 0.64.4: check `swiftformat --version` matches, or use the Docker image `ghcr.io/nicklockwood/swiftformat:0.64.4`.
{% endif %}
## Set up GitHub (once)

After the first commit, the repo owner (admin) runs `scripts/setup-github.sh --public`: it creates the repo, pushes, and sets merge settings and `main` protection.
Pick a license first; this template adds none.

## Template updates

`scripts/update-from-template.sh` pulls in the latest template on a branch and opens a PR.
